# Cloudflare Pages redirects for ember.deepanswerlabs.com
#
# THE ONE PLACE TO CHANGE WHERE DOWNLOADS POINT. Every download button on the site
# links to a stable /download/* path on this domain; this file maps those paths to
# wherever the binaries actually live. Moving hosting (GitHub Releases -> R2, a
# different repo, a CDN) is an edit here and a redeploy, never an HTML change.
#
# Hosting today: GitHub Releases, via .../releases/latest/download/<file>, which
# GitHub resolves to the newest non-draft, non-prerelease release. That only works
# because electron-builder.yml gives the artifacts version-free names; every release
# must upload exactly these three files.
#
# The public repo is afetiu/ember-terminal. If it moves (a Deep Answer Labs org),
# change owner/repo below and REPO_URL in site/main.js together.
#
# If the binaries move to R2 instead, point these at the bucket's public/custom-domain
# URL, e.g. https://dl.deepanswerlabs.com/ember/latest/Ember-Setup-win-x64.exe
#
# 302 (not 301) on purpose: browsers cache 301s forever, and "latest" changes.

/download/windows          https://github.com/afetiu/ember-terminal/releases/latest/download/Ember-Setup-win-x64.exe  302
/download/windows-zip      https://github.com/afetiu/ember-terminal/releases/latest/download/Ember-win-x64.zip        302
/download/windows-targz    https://github.com/afetiu/ember-terminal/releases/latest/download/Ember-win-x64.tar.gz     302

# Convenience aliases.
/download                  /download/windows  302
/download/windows/         /download/windows  302
